Provide comprehensive, accurate, and medically sound information about the drug "{{$drug_name}}".
All medical information MUST be written in professional Arabic.

Use the `get_drug_info` tool to look up the drug in the PharmaLink database first.
Then, combine that data with your medical knowledge to produce a structured response.

## Required Output Format (always respond in JSON matching this schema exactly):
{
  "drugName": "string — official name as found in database or corrected spelling",
  "arabicName": "string or null — the Arabic name of the drug from the database",
  "genericName": "string or null — the International Non-proprietary Name (INN)",
  "category": "string — therapeutic category (e.g. Antibiotic, NSAID, Antihypertensive) in Arabic",
  "description": "string — 2-3 sentences explaining what the drug is and how it works (in Arabic)",
  "indications": "string — what conditions it is used to treat (in Arabic)",
  "contraindications": "string — who should NOT take it (pregnancy, kidney disease, etc.) (in Arabic)",
  "sideEffects": "string — common and serious side effects (in Arabic)",
  "dosage": "string — typical adult dosage guidance (in Arabic)",
  "storageInstructions": "string — how to store the drug (in Arabic)",
  "requiresPrescription": true or false,
  "isAvailableInSystem": true or false — based on the database lookup result
}

## Rules:
- Base factual claims on established pharmacological knowledge.
- If the database lookup fails, set isAvailableInSystem to false but still provide general medical info.
- Never omit any field — use null for truly unknown values.
- Do not include markdown fences or explanatory text — return ONLY the JSON object.
